STATIC METHOD:-

A static method in Python is a method defined inside a class that does not depend on any instance or class data. It is used when a function logically belongs to a class but does not need access to self or cls. Static methods help organize related utility functions inside a class without creating objects.
It behaves like a normal function but is logically grouped inside a class for better organization.
Static method can be inheroted by child class


class calculation:
    @staticmethod
    def sum(a,b):
        return (a+b)

    def sub(a,b):
        return(a-b)

print("Sum of a and b: ",calculation.sum(10,5))
print("Sub of a and b: ",calculation.sub(10,5))


# it is possible but it is not meant and it is decurased not to be used

obj=calculation()
print(obj.sum(10,8))


